"""Build the NSW CTP severity causal DAG.

Emits ``causal/ctp_causal_dag.json`` — the machine-readable structure consumed by
the causal (DAG-aware) TabPFN generator described in
``specs/nsw-ctp-causative.md``.

PROVENANCE — READ THIS BEFORE RELYING ON THE GRAPH.
The edge list, the signs, the strengths and the mechanism strings below were
**generated by a large language model** (Claude) from its training knowledge of
NSW CTP scheme mechanics (Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017 / Motor Accidents
Compensation Act 1999 heads of damage).  **No lawyer, actuary or claims
practitioner has reviewed any edge.**  Earlier versions of this file described
the graph as "expert-elicited"; that was inaccurate and has been corrected.

The graph is then **annotated** with the empirical association each edge carries
in ``ctp/ctp.csv``.  The associations do not orient the edges, and they cannot
validate them — a plausible-sounding wrong arrow will still carry a correlation.
They are reported so a reader can see which asserted mechanisms the data is at
least consistent with.

The descriptive statistics quoted inside the ``note`` and ``mechanism`` strings
are checked against the CSV by ``causal/verify_claims.py``.  The causal
assertions themselves are unverified and unfalsifiable from 540 observational
rows; they need domain review.

Run:  python causal/build_ctp_causal_dag.py
"""

